{title: Love Is Patient}
{subtitle: 1 Corinthians 13}
{key: D}
{tempo: 71}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [D] | [D] | [D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
If I speak in the tongues of men and [Bm7]of angels
But have [G]not love
I am [D]a noisy gong, a clanging cym[Bm7]bal
If I have all faith, so as to remove [G]mountains
But have not love, [D]I am nothing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Love is patient, [D]love is kind
Love never ends
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Love does not envy or boast
[Bm7]It is not arrogant or rude
[G]It does not insist on its own way
It [D]bears all things, believes all things
[Bm7]Hopes all things, endures all things [G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Love is patient, love is [D]kind
Love never ends
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
For now we see in a mirror dimly
[Bm7]But then face to face
[G]Now I know in part, then I shall know fully
[D]So now faith, hope and love abide, these [G]three
But the greatest of these is [D]love
{end_of_verse}
